# Default tool allowlist for ad-hoc queued tasks.
#
# Read-only by construction, the same principle the daily email scan follows:
# an unattended run physically cannot send mail, move files, or execute a shell
# even if the prompt is misread or the task text is not what you meant.
#
# Results reach the vault via the runner, which writes Claude's output into
# 00_Inbox/Agent_Results/ itself — no task needs Write to produce a note.
#
# Grant anything beyond this per task, with `ct -t`, and only when you mean it:
#   Write,Edit          let the task modify vault notes directly
#   Bash                let the task execute shell on lab01
#   mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__send_message   let it mail out

# --- reading the vault and the web ---
Read
Glob
Grep
WebFetch
WebSearch

# --- Gmail: search and read only, no send/reply/trash/label ---
mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__search_threads
mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__get_thread

# --- Calendar: read only, no create/update/delete ---
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__list_events
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__search_events
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__list_calendars

# --- Drive: read only ---
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__search_files
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__read_file_content

# --- headless browser, for pages that need rendering ---
mcp__playwright__browser_navigate
mcp__playwright__browser_snapshot
